        "id": "F1",
        "severity": "WARNING",
        "location": "engine/runtime/memorycard-opencode-plugin.mjs:222-231",
        "claim": "Session eviction is insertion-order (FIFO), not LRU, and child sessions also take a slot, because the context hook fires for them and sessionOf creates an entry before the child check. A long-lived main session is therefore forgotten after 128 newer sessions. Subagent-heavy work can reach that count. Its next model call then asks memorycard again, and the system prompt changes mid-session. That is exactly what the commit's cache-stability goal says must not happen. Even when the text is unchanged, the entry is lost. If memorycard fails on the re-ask, the block disappears mid-session.",
        "evidence_class": "inferential",
        "causal_disposition": "introduced",
        "proof_refs": [
          "engine/runtime/memorycard-opencode-plugin.mjs:222-231",
          "engine/runtime/opencode_memorycard_plugin_test.go:462-470"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "F2",
        "severity": "SUGGESTION",
        "location": "engine/runtime/memorycard-opencode-plugin.mjs:139-170",
        "claim": "The capture timeout sends only SIGTERM, with no SIGKILL escalation (runMemorycard has one). A memorycard that ignores SIGTERM stays running, detached. Captures are also unbounded in concurrency while they are not paused. `ctx.session.get` inside `isChildSession` has no timeout, so a hung call would block every model call of that session.",
        "evidence_class": "inferential",
        "causal_disposition": "introduced",
        "proof_refs": [
